WEBVTT

00:03.380 --> 00:04.460
Grandpa?

00:04.460 --> 00:06.360
Enough!

00:06.360 --> 00:09.230
I told you, this is not for sale!

00:09.880 --> 00:14.690
I poured my heart and soul into each and 
every single one of the goods here.

00:14.690 --> 00:17.340
They're unlike anything 
you can buy anywhere else!

00:17.340 --> 00:20.490
I would never sell them to a youngster 
who can't understand their real value!

00:20.920 --> 00:23.560
Got it? Now scram!

00:23.560 --> 00:26.250
What an annoying old man you are.

00:26.690 --> 00:29.880
Just tell me how much you want for it, then.

00:30.860 --> 00:32.760
It's not a matter of money—

00:33.820 --> 00:36.510
Grandpa, is he a complainer?

00:36.510 --> 00:37.560
Indeed!

00:37.560 --> 00:38.660
No!

00:38.660 --> 00:41.640
He's interfering with my 
business, that's what!

00:42.610 --> 00:45.020
Then this should cover it, right?

00:45.880 --> 00:48.050
Like I said, I won't take 
your spare change...

00:49.940 --> 00:51.030
Sold!

00:57.750 --> 00:58.910
Grandpa.

00:59.610 --> 01:03.540
I thought you said pride is the most 
important thing for a craftsman.

01:04.960 --> 01:06.290
That's right.

01:06.830 --> 01:11.170
Pride and attention to detail are 
very important for a craftsman.

01:11.890 --> 01:15.050
If you lose sight of them, you'll get nowhere.

01:16.700 --> 01:18.340
That said, Ruri...

01:25.770 --> 01:28.060
Sometimes, there are exceptions.

01:31.680 --> 01:33.630
This is one of those exceptions.

02:02.740 --> 02:05.580
<i>I loved my grandpa deeply, 
and this was his last job.</i>

02:06.480 --> 02:09.060
<i>I'll see it through to the end, 
no matter what!</i>

02:29.680 --> 02:31.170
H-Hey!

02:36.000 --> 02:39.120
What's the matter? Please don't stop!

02:44.650 --> 02:45.610
Could it be...

03:01.720 --> 03:02.700
The brooch!

03:13.180 --> 03:14.710
Thank goodness.

03:17.990 --> 03:24.910
If I'd lost this, Grandpa 
would have haunted me.

03:24.910 --> 03:26.930
Anyway, time to go...

03:29.640 --> 03:31.860
U-Um, you know...

03:31.860 --> 03:35.630
I'm all bony, and I'd taste terrible.

03:35.630 --> 03:38.840
You can have all the food you want, so, um,

03:38.840 --> 03:41.990
please, could you find it 
in your heart to let me...

03:42.350 --> 03:45.420
Oh, I know! I have money! 
Let's settle this with money—

05:21.500 --> 05:25.970
<b><i>Episode 2</i></b>

05:21.500 --> 05:25.970
<b><i>Going on a Trip for a Second Time</i></b>

05:38.620 --> 05:41.150
Yikes, this is bad.

05:42.030 --> 05:43.150
You okay?

05:44.980 --> 05:47.280
I-Is it money you want?

05:47.540 --> 05:53.380
To tell you the truth, I don't have any 
cash on hand until I deliver these items.

05:53.380 --> 05:56.510
If you could write an invoice, 
I can set up an account and—

05:56.510 --> 05:59.290
There's no need for that. 
I was just passing through.

05:59.850 --> 06:01.540
As long as you're safe, it's fine.

06:02.030 --> 06:04.120
But my grandpa used to say,

06:04.120 --> 06:09.650
"There's no such thing as a free lunch, 
so settle everything with money," so...

06:10.630 --> 06:13.560
Your grandpa sounds like trash.

06:21.230 --> 06:22.190
What?

06:23.040 --> 06:25.690
Oh, it's nothing!

06:27.350 --> 06:32.000
Someone like you carrying goods 
without a guard? Sounds crazy.

06:32.000 --> 06:36.000
I had to leave in a rush, so I couldn't 
find anyone who would take the job.

06:37.470 --> 06:42.640
Well, just remember that money isn't 
going to do you any good if you die.

06:42.640 --> 06:43.430
See ya.

06:44.940 --> 06:49.840
W-Wait! Could you please be my guard, then?!

06:49.840 --> 06:52.220
I promise to pay you!

06:52.530 --> 06:56.720
Sorry, I've got my own errands 
to run. Find someone else.

06:56.720 --> 07:00.350
Please! Just part of the way is fine!

07:01.120 --> 07:06.360
I really have to deliver 
this package! Please!

07:12.800 --> 07:15.680
All right. Until we get to 
that port town up ahead.

07:15.680 --> 07:17.200
And you don't have to pay me.

07:23.550 --> 07:26.940
Oh, my goods...

07:26.940 --> 07:27.880
Let it go.

07:28.720 --> 07:32.050
I only agreed to being your guard, 
not your porter.

07:32.740 --> 07:34.710
I know, but...

07:38.680 --> 07:41.480
Is that your precious package?

07:41.480 --> 07:42.520
I won't show you!

07:42.520 --> 07:44.270
I don't want to see.

07:44.790 --> 07:47.930
This is really, truly precious!

07:47.930 --> 07:51.250
I can't show you, Setsu-san, 
even if you're my guard!

07:51.250 --> 07:53.800
Like I said, I didn't ask to see it...

07:57.030 --> 07:59.040
Welcome!

07:59.400 --> 08:01.040
They're all fresh!

08:01.640 --> 08:03.100
Over here!

08:03.690 --> 08:04.540
It's delicious!

08:05.720 --> 08:06.750
Awesome!

08:06.750 --> 08:08.050
And then my wife said...

08:08.050 --> 08:13.550
<b>Marsenne, Port Town</b>

08:08.590 --> 08:11.620
Wow, this town grew quite a bit.

08:13.760 --> 08:19.160
After the war ended five years ago,
 trade went up by a lot.

08:19.160 --> 08:21.430
Have you been here before, Setsu-san?

08:21.430 --> 08:24.060
Yeah, back before the trade went up.

08:26.160 --> 08:30.020
Anyway, I've hired a ship to take me from here!

08:30.020 --> 08:32.190
A ship to the demonic continent?

08:33.600 --> 08:34.860
No way we're going there.

08:36.870 --> 08:38.760
Oh, no...

08:38.760 --> 08:42.650
There's a war going on. Obviously every 
ship is canceled for the foreseeable future.

08:43.430 --> 08:45.140
What can I do?

08:45.140 --> 08:49.630
You were trying to go to the demonic 
continent in this day and age?

08:50.060 --> 08:52.330
Obviously that's impossible.

08:52.330 --> 08:54.160
But my package...

09:02.430 --> 09:05.760
Um, can you ferry me to 
the demonic continent?!

09:05.760 --> 09:08.810
Are you crazy, little girl? No way.

09:09.940 --> 09:13.100
Please let me take your ship 
to the demonic continent!

09:13.100 --> 09:16.680
You're kidding, right? 
Out of my way. I have work to do.

09:17.330 --> 09:18.750
Please!

09:18.750 --> 09:21.190
Sorry, but a no is a no.

09:31.830 --> 09:34.920
Ugh... Okay, fine!

09:36.270 --> 09:38.700
Hey, you there! Halt!

09:38.700 --> 09:39.910
Y-Yes, sir!

09:44.060 --> 09:46.860
We are the Knights of Distinia.

09:46.860 --> 09:49.560
We're conducting inspections 
for the safety of the port.

09:49.920 --> 09:52.440
If you're a merchant, show me 
your identification documents.

09:52.440 --> 09:54.150
Oh, y-yes, sir.

09:58.050 --> 10:02.890
Hmph. While we soldiers 
put our lives on the line,

10:02.890 --> 10:05.710
you folk chase after money.

10:05.710 --> 10:09.400
Women and children playing merchant?

10:09.400 --> 10:11.210
I envy your freedom.

10:11.210 --> 10:15.710
Oh, sorry... I'm fortunate enough to get by...

10:18.870 --> 10:20.970
Hey, show us that leather bag.

10:20.970 --> 10:22.930
N-Not this!

10:26.110 --> 10:30.440
N-No, this is just a really important 
piece of merchandise, so...

10:30.440 --> 10:33.550
If it's merchandise, then why hide it?

10:33.550 --> 10:35.010
That's suspicious.

10:35.010 --> 10:39.660
For disobeying us knights, 
we're confiscating that bag!

10:45.410 --> 10:48.800
Inspecting packages in broad daylight?

10:48.800 --> 10:52.440
Do you have the right permits for that?

10:52.850 --> 10:54.380
Who are you?

10:54.380 --> 10:56.710
Her guard. You got a problem with that?

10:56.710 --> 11:02.430
Oh? So a mere adventurer like you 
dares to challenge the royal knights?

11:02.810 --> 11:04.160
Even if it's for your owner,

11:04.160 --> 11:07.060
you should be careful when 
choosing who to bite.

11:07.060 --> 11:11.430
Interesting. Draw if you dare.

11:11.430 --> 11:12.600
Setsu-san!

11:14.130 --> 11:15.820
H-Hey, over here!

11:16.680 --> 11:19.990
Look, the military police are at it again.

11:19.990 --> 11:23.320
Are they drawing their swords? For real?

11:25.640 --> 11:28.030
We won't forget this. Let's go.

11:28.700 --> 11:33.710
One wrong move and we're locking you up.

11:37.330 --> 11:40.760
It must be tough for Elka and Glein,

11:40.760 --> 11:43.080
if they have to keep folk like them in line.

11:43.490 --> 11:44.850
Setsu-san!

11:44.850 --> 11:48.120
Thank you so much!

11:49.350 --> 11:50.380
Ouch...

11:50.380 --> 11:53.770
How much do I owe you 
for that wonderful service?!

11:51.880 --> 11:55.080
Not my neck! Hey, stop!

11:56.420 --> 11:58.460
I get it! I get it, okay?!

12:12.620 --> 12:17.730
You were so awesome back there, Setsu-san!

12:17.730 --> 12:21.010
Please have as many as you want! It's on me!

12:21.510 --> 12:23.320
I was impressed, too.

12:23.320 --> 12:26.310
You kept a smile on your face, even 
though they were being stupid bullies.

12:26.310 --> 12:27.510
You're a real pro.

12:29.590 --> 12:31.270
Thank you for the compliment.

12:32.640 --> 12:34.010
But, Setsu-san...

12:34.010 --> 12:38.240
How did you know they needed a permit 
to search personal belongings?

12:38.770 --> 12:43.270
Only soldiers with badges 
can question civilians.

12:43.270 --> 12:46.940
An old friend knew a lot about that stuff, 
and he was a real stickler for rules.

12:48.280 --> 12:53.330
But if you can't find a ship, 
you can't go any farther.

12:53.330 --> 12:54.410
What are you gonna do?

12:57.530 --> 13:01.770
I'll search the entire town to see 
if anyone can send out a ship.

13:02.330 --> 13:04.110
If that doesn't work...

13:04.110 --> 13:05.430
Then?

13:05.430 --> 13:06.930
I'll buy a ship.

13:07.240 --> 13:08.180
That's impossible.

13:08.780 --> 13:11.350
Do you know how much that would cost?

13:11.350 --> 13:13.430
It doesn't matter how much.

13:19.930 --> 13:21.920
I do have one idea.

13:22.560 --> 13:26.980
R-Really?! How much would it cost?!

13:26.980 --> 13:30.100
I was on my way to the 
demonic continent anyway,

13:30.100 --> 13:31.580
so there's no need to pay me.

13:32.760 --> 13:33.830
But...

13:34.240 --> 13:36.310
You have to rest at an inn tonight.

13:36.310 --> 13:37.910
That's the condition.

13:37.910 --> 13:40.210
I'm grateful for your concern, but...

13:40.490 --> 13:44.310
You're so tired, you can't even eat. 
Don't push yourself so hard.

13:49.900 --> 13:51.470
Setsu-san...

13:52.340 --> 13:53.630
Okay, let's go.

13:53.630 --> 13:54.660
Yes!

13:54.660 --> 13:56.480
Oh, just one thing...

13:56.480 --> 13:57.230
What is it?

13:57.660 --> 13:59.980
Can we split the cost for the inn?

14:19.450 --> 14:21.240
That felt great.

14:21.240 --> 14:23.130
The bath's free. Go wash up, Ruri.

14:23.400 --> 14:24.150
Okay.

14:27.240 --> 14:30.090
Man, that was heavenly.

14:30.090 --> 14:31.730
Um, Setsu-san...

14:35.410 --> 14:40.770
While I'm in the bath, 
can you hold on to this?

14:41.710 --> 14:44.770
Are you sure? Isn't that precious to you?

14:45.110 --> 14:45.920
Yes.

14:46.930 --> 14:48.380
But I'll show you.

14:51.730 --> 14:57.040
This is the last job that my grandpa took on.

15:00.300 --> 15:01.650
<i>This brooch...</i>

15:04.840 --> 15:09.050
Let me tell you a bit about my grandpa.

15:15.320 --> 15:19.060
My grandpa was a famous jeweler.

15:21.240 --> 15:28.160
I heard nobody else in Distinia could 
make what my grandpa could make.

15:30.440 --> 15:33.980
One day, someone came in to 
request a repair for a brooch

15:33.980 --> 15:36.760
that my grandpa had made, 
which he was most proud of.

15:38.400 --> 15:39.080
But...

15:42.010 --> 15:46.460
He didn't have much time left.

15:54.860 --> 15:59.670
Ruri, I taught you that money is important,

15:59.670 --> 16:04.350
but that's only because you need it to 
protect what is most important to you.

16:04.900 --> 16:09.110
Without money, you can't 
protect what's most important.

16:09.670 --> 16:13.330
Being able to give up 
everything else in order to

16:13.330 --> 16:18.270
protect what's most important to you...
That's what true pride is.

16:18.270 --> 16:19.580
Grandpa...

16:20.220 --> 16:21.120
Ruri...

16:22.200 --> 16:26.880
Can I trust you with my final job?

16:32.660 --> 16:33.630
Yes!

16:33.970 --> 16:36.960
It'll be okay! It really will!

16:37.730 --> 16:41.130
I'll deliver it, I promise!

16:44.320 --> 16:49.850
So, as my grandpa's apprentice, 
and as his granddaughter,

16:49.850 --> 16:52.570
I want to deliver this brooch safely.

16:53.330 --> 16:54.650
Please.

17:00.580 --> 17:02.690
I'm taking that bath now.

17:04.570 --> 17:07.600
Please don't take my money!

17:11.120 --> 17:12.510
<i>Dear Grandpa.</i>

17:12.510 --> 17:14.540
<i>Thanks to someone very kind,</i>

17:14.540 --> 17:16.540
<i>I think I'll be able to keep our promise.</i>

17:30.550 --> 17:34.940
<i>I knew it. This is the brooch 
I cast protection magic on.</i>

17:35.990 --> 17:37.950
<i>This broke?</i>

17:43.570 --> 17:46.360
<i>I hope nothing bad happened...</i>

18:01.970 --> 18:06.940
Sirs?! H-How can I help you?

18:07.330 --> 18:11.500
Where is the merchant girl and the 
guard with the big, black sword?!

18:11.500 --> 18:14.980
They are suspected of spying for the demons!

18:14.980 --> 18:17.700
Hiding them would do you no good!

18:21.920 --> 18:25.010
Seriously? You'd go this far?

18:25.720 --> 18:28.330
Breakfast already?

18:29.170 --> 18:31.340
Here they are! In this room!

18:33.460 --> 18:36.190
We'll have to bump up our departure time a bit.

18:36.190 --> 18:36.920
Let's go!

18:45.700 --> 18:48.110
They escaped through the window! After them!

18:49.440 --> 18:51.010
Over here! This way!

18:51.010 --> 18:52.240
No, that way!

18:52.240 --> 18:53.030
No, this way!

18:53.120 --> 18:53.980
No, this way!

18:54.060 --> 18:54.940
No, this way!

18:54.940 --> 18:56.690
Wait, which way?

18:59.520 --> 19:01.200
I see them! This way!

19:01.200 --> 19:04.700
Wow, so diligent for so late at night.

19:11.380 --> 19:13.600
In the alley! Corner them!

19:20.380 --> 19:23.810
Oh, dear. Seems like there's 
a lot of trash in these parts.

19:33.430 --> 19:34.380
Huh?

19:35.260 --> 19:39.110
S-Setsu-san! This is a dead end!

19:39.110 --> 19:41.090
What are we going to do?!

19:41.090 --> 19:42.700
We're in trouble.

19:42.700 --> 19:44.370
Found them!

19:46.560 --> 19:48.310
There's nowhere else to run!

19:48.310 --> 19:50.620
You caused us a lot of trouble!

19:50.620 --> 19:53.370
You won't apologize 
your way out of this one!

19:53.760 --> 19:57.330
I've got no apologies for goons like you!

19:57.330 --> 19:59.510
Stop being scared and bring it on!

19:59.510 --> 20:03.010
Hey! Why do you have to provoke them?!

20:04.220 --> 20:07.010
Okay, it's about time we took our leave.

20:07.010 --> 20:09.400
Huh? Now? What—

20:11.640 --> 20:12.520
H-Hey!

20:16.150 --> 20:18.480
Am I flying?!

20:18.890 --> 20:19.970
No way.

20:19.970 --> 20:20.740
They're gonna die!

20:21.160 --> 20:23.990
F-Fall... falling... falling!

20:23.990 --> 20:27.240
Long time no see! I'm back!

20:34.790 --> 20:36.010
Levia!

20:41.330 --> 20:43.650
Sorry for the short notice, Levia.

20:43.650 --> 20:47.940
I'll fill you in later, but can you 
take us over to the demonic continent?

20:58.360 --> 21:01.780
Um, how do we report this?

21:02.230 --> 21:05.610
W-We had a dream.

21:05.610 --> 21:09.600
And we don't report dreams... Right?

21:20.980 --> 21:22.880
Levia?

21:23.280 --> 21:26.020
Leviathan, the god of the ocean?

21:30.840 --> 21:35.630
<i>Who in the world did I hire as my guard?</i>

21:45.890 --> 21:47.410
It's in sight now.

21:48.520 --> 21:51.680
The demonic continent, at last!

23:27.000 --> 23:32.010
<b><i>Next Time</i></b>

23:27.000 --> 23:32.010
<b><i>Frying a Squid for a Second Time</i></b>

23:27.830 --> 23:31.100
Next time: "Frying a Squid for a Second Time."
